cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Si utiliza este software, por favor cítelo como se indica a continuación. / If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Meritum_CAT: Scientific Platform for Computerized Adaptive Testing, Psychometric Modeling and Assessment Simulation"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-25"
authors:
  - family-names: "Gómez Otero"
    given-names: "Keidy Lucía"
  - family-names: "Burgos Flórez"
    given-names: "Francisco Javier"
    email: "fjburgosf@gmail.com"
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/primbiolab/Meritum_CAT"
abstract: >-
  Meritum_CAT is a bilingual (Spanish/English) desktop scientific platform for research on
  computerized adaptive testing based on item response theory. It implements the 1PL/Rasch, 2PL and
  3PL models, MLE, MAP and EAP ability estimation, maximum Fisher information, random, randomesque,
  Kullback-Leibler and Sympson-Hetter item selection, configurable stopping rules, content balancing,
  item exposure analysis, reproducible Monte Carlo simulation and ten predefined computational
  experiments, with scientific visualization and exportable, reproducible experiment configurations.
keywords:
  - psychometrics
  - item response theory
  - computerized adaptive testing
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - reproducibility
